{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albert-einshutoin/qzt/pulls/286","id":4109884224,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSzopF87099tA","html_url":"https://github.com/albert-einshutoin/qzt/pull/286","diff_url":"https://github.com/albert-einshutoin/qzt/pull/286.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/albert-einshutoin/qzt/pull/286.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albert-einshutoin/qzt/issues/286","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albert-einshutoin/qzt/pulls/286/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albert-einshutoin/qzt/pulls/286/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albert-einshutoin/qzt/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albert-einshutoin/qzt/issues/286/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albert-einshutoin/qzt/statuses/16033d45bfc96b7b43011e597c302a650d026efc","number":286,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"ci: add fail-safe impact-selected PR tests","user":{"login":"albert-einshutoin","id":75466198,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1NDY2MTk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75466198?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/albert-einshutoin","html_url":"https://github.com/albert-einshutoin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albert-einshutoin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albert-einshutoin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albert-einshutoin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albert-einshutoin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albert-einshutoin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albert-einshutoin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albert-einshutoin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albert-einshutoin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albert-einshutoin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Why\n\nPR CI currently runs the complete Rust suite on every change and repeats that work in coverage, even when a change has a bounded module or documentation impact. This increases elapsed time and billed compute. The optimization must not reduce failure detection when impact analysis is uncertain.\n\n## Before\n\n- Both stable and MSRV `check` lanes ran `make check`, including the full test suite.\n- PR coverage ran the complete suite again.\n- There was no machine-readable explanation of which tests were relevant or why full validation was required.\n- Main was the only post-merge CI branch and there was no daily/manual full validation lane in `ci.yml`.\n\n## After\n\n- PRs always run formatting, Clippy, all-target compilation, docs, package, dependency policy, Windows release checks, public-example smoke, and security workflows.\n- A CI-service-neutral planner reads rename/copy/delete-aware Git diffs, applies centralized dangerous-file rules, traverses reverse Rust module dependencies, recognizes public re-exports, and supplements them with explicit module/path mappings.\n- Rust-specific analysis and commands live in `ci/adapters/`; the common planner contains no Rust dependency parser.\n- Selected plans always add smoke tests. Missing revisions, malformed configuration, unknown files, stale mappings, shared contracts, dependency/build/test/CI changes, or analysis errors select the full suite.\n- Main/release pushes, daily schedules, and manual dispatches force full validation. Full coverage remains on those lanes and is removed only from PRs to avoid executing all tests twice.\n- Plans and execution summaries are uploaded for 14 days with revisions, changed/deleted files, affected modules, targets, fallback reason, target results, and duration.\n\n## Key decisions\n\n- Selected Cargo targets run sequentially in one job because parallel hosted jobs would duplicate compilation and can increase total compute cost for this single-crate repository.\n- Adapter commands are argv arrays and selected target names are allowlisted, so changed filenames are never interpreted by a shell.\n- Adapter corruption fails CI because no trustworthy full command can be recovered; impact-policy corruption produces a full plan.\n- This PR changes CI policy itself, so its own impact plan intentionally falls back to the full suite.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `make check`\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s ci/tests -v` — 18 passed\n- planner + adapter runner against `origin/main...HEAD` — full fallback, 0 failed, 21.9s\n- `gitleaks detect --source . --no-git --redact --exit-code 1` — no leaks\n- `cargo deny check bans licenses sources` — all checks passed; existing unmatched NCSA allowance warning only\n- `git diff --check`\n\n## Documentation\n\n- Added English and Japanese selective-CI architecture and maintenance guides.\n- Linked the new contract from both contributor guides.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-07-22T16:23:19Z","updated_at":"2026-09-27T16:19:24Z","closed_at":"2026-09-27T16:19:24Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"edb0bb2f83e50efa78f154c184885ea04dce70af","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"albert-einshutoin:feat/selective-test-ci","ref":"feat/selective-test-ci","repo":{"id":1262102807,"node_id":"R_kgDOSzopFw","name":"qzt","full_name":"albert-einshutoin/qzt","owner":{"login":"albert-einshutoin","id":75466198,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1NDY2MTk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75466198?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/albert-einshutoin","html_url":"https://github.com/albert-einshutoin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albert-einshutoin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albert-einshutoin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albert-einshutoin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.gith